WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

2
00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:10.630
Are you
sure about this?

3
00:02:10.922 --> 00:02:12.423
No.

4
00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.676
It's dangerous.

5
00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:20.097
If we take Tywin's castle from him.

6
00:02:20.182 --> 00:02:23.434
the lords of Westeros
will realize he's not invincible.

7
00:02:23.852 --> 00:02:26.937
Take his home. take his
gold. take his power.

8
00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.273
Why are you telling me?

9
00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.820
You begged me not to send Theon

10
00:02:34.905 --> 00:02:38.699
to negotiate with his father.
and I ignored your advice.

11
00:02:40.744 --> 00:02:43.037
Now Winterfell is burnt to the ground.

12
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:47.083
the North is overrun with ironborn.
and Bran and Rickon are gone.

13
00:02:50.212 --> 00:02:51.712
So. Casterly Rock...

14
00:02:56.343 --> 00:02:57.927
I'm asking your advice.

15
00:03:04.476 --> 00:03:06.936
We have enough men?

16
00:03:10.107 --> 00:03:15.236
If Walder Frey cooperates.

17
00:03:20.242 --> 00:03:25.705
If reinforcements arrive from King's
Landing before we take the castle.

18
00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.835
we'll be caught between
Tywin's army and the sea.

19
00:03:35.507 --> 00:03:39.593
We'll lose the war and
die the way Father died.

20
00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:41.345
Or worse.

21
00:03:46.101 --> 00:03:49.562
Show them how it feels
to lose what they love.

22
00:04:20.343 --> 00:04:23.012
My honored guests.

23
00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:28.267
be welcome within my walls and at my table.

24
00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:33.147
I extend to you my hospitality

25
00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:37.026
and protection in the light of the Seven.

26
00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.528
We thank you for your hospitality. my lord.

27
00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:48.537
I have come to make my apologies. my
lord. and to beg your forgiveness.

28
00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:52.041
Don't beg my forgiveness. Your Grace.

29
00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:56.378
It wasn't me you spurned. It was my girls.

30
00:05:08.892 --> 00:05:11.393
One of them was supposed to be queen.

31
00:05:11.478 --> 00:05:13.020
Now none of them are.

32
00:05:14.689 --> 00:05:18.150
This is Arwyn. my daughter.

33
00:05:18.235 --> 00:05:22.822
My daughter Walda. my daughter Derwa.

34
00:05:22.906 --> 00:05:25.449
my daughter Waldra.

35
00:05:29.871 --> 00:05:35.084
My eldest granddaughters Ginia and Neila.

36
00:05:36.962 --> 00:05:41.215
Serra and Sarra. granddaughters. twins.

37
00:05:41.258 --> 00:05:42.967
You could have had either.

38
00:05:43.593 --> 00:05:46.220
Could have had both. for all I care.

39
00:05:46.555 --> 00:05:48.597
My granddaughter Marianne.

40
00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:51.684
My granddaughter Freya.

41
00:05:52.811 --> 00:05:54.478
My granddaughter...

42
00:05:55.814 --> 00:05:56.856
Wertha.

43
00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:00.860
Waldra.

44
00:06:02.988 --> 00:06:04.321
Waldina.

45
00:06:04.573 --> 00:06:05.573
I'm Merry.

46
00:06:05.615 --> 00:06:07.324
Fine.

47
00:06:07.409 --> 00:06:11.036
And here's my youngest daughter Shirei.

48
00:06:12.289 --> 00:06:13.914
though she hasn't bled yet.

49
00:06:14.457 --> 00:06:16.584
Clearly you don't have
the patience for all that.

50
00:06:18.461 --> 00:06:19.795
My ladies.

51
00:06:19.963 --> 00:06:23.173
All men should
keep their word. kings most of all.

52
00:06:24.718 --> 00:06:27.845
I was pledged to
marry one of you and I broke that vow.

53
00:06:27.929 --> 00:06:30.014
The fault is not with you.

54
00:06:30.098 --> 00:06:32.349
Any man would be lucky
to have any one of you.

55
00:06:33.685 --> 00:06:38.397
I did what I did not to slight
you. but because I loved another.

56
00:06:38.481 --> 00:06:40.316
I know these words cannot set right

57
00:06:40.442 --> 00:06:42.276
the wrong I have done
to you and your house.

58
00:06:43.278 --> 00:06:44.778
I beg your forgiveness

59
00:06:45.947 --> 00:06:50.159
and pledge to do all I can to make
amends so the Freys of the Crossing

60
00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:52.703
and the Starks of Winterfell
may once again be friends.

61
00:07:01.171 --> 00:07:03.005
Very good.

62
00:07:05.175 --> 00:07:06.425
There she is.

63
00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:11.055
Come closer. Let me have a look at you.

64
00:07:17.938 --> 00:07:19.605
Still can't see you.

65
00:07:20.565 --> 00:07:22.191
Old eyes.

66
00:07:37.582 --> 00:07:39.500
Love.

67
00:07:39.542 --> 00:07:43.170
That's what the Starks of
Winterfell call it. eh?

68
00:07:45.632 --> 00:07:49.510
Very honorable. I call it a pretty face.

69
00:07:49.552 --> 00:07:50.594
Mmm.

70
00:07:51.638 --> 00:07:52.680
Very pretty.

71
00:07:54.808 --> 00:07:56.850
Prettier than this lot. that's for sure.

72
00:07:58.728 --> 00:08:00.437
Very shapely as well.

73
00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:05.275
Oh. you try to hide her under that dress.

74
00:08:05.944 --> 00:08:07.069
If you wanted to hide her.

75
00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:09.446
you shouldn't have
brought her here in the first place.

76
00:08:15.996 --> 00:08:20.332
I can always see
what's going on beneath a dress.

77
00:08:20.625 --> 00:08:22.751
Been at this a long time.

78
00:08:24.587 --> 00:08:27.172
I bet when you take that dress off.

79
00:08:27.298 --> 00:08:29.925
everything stays right where it is.

80
00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:31.427
Doesn't drop an inch.

81
00:08:33.638 --> 00:08:36.181
Your king says he betrayed me for love.

82
00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:41.353
I say he betrayed
me for firm tits and a tight fit.

83
00:08:42.856 --> 00:08:45.149
And I can respect that.

84
00:08:46.943 --> 00:08:50.237
When I was your age.
I'd have broken 50 oaths

85
00:08:50.363 --> 00:08:53.657
to get into that without a second thought.

86
00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:00.831
Well. I've enough room
in the hall for you lot.

87
00:09:00.915 --> 00:09:05.127
We'll set up tents outside
with food and ale for the rest of your men.

88
00:09:05.628 --> 00:09:07.129
Thank you. my lord.

89
00:09:10.884 --> 00:09:11.967
Well. let's get ready.

90
00:09:12.594 --> 00:09:14.344
The wine will flow red

91
00:09:15.472 --> 00:09:17.806
and the music will play loud

92
00:09:18.183 --> 00:09:22.144
and we'll put this mess behind us.

93
00:09:31.321 --> 00:09:32.613
Where?

94
00:09:32.655 --> 00:09:34.156
There.

95
00:09:41.664 --> 00:09:44.666
There. It's a back gate.

96
00:09:44.709 --> 00:09:47.169
My men use it
when they visit Yunkai's bed slaves.

97
00:09:47.212 --> 00:09:48.879
Your men. but not you?

98
00:09:49.005 --> 00:09:50.672
I have no interest in slaves.

99
00:09:50.715 --> 00:09:52.841
A man cannot make love to property.

100
00:09:56.513 --> 00:09:59.431
This is where we enter
the city. Very few guards. They know me.

101
00:09:59.724 --> 00:10:00.849
They let me inside...

102
00:10:00.892 --> 00:10:03.143
We're not gonna
sneak an army through a back gate.

103
00:10:03.186 --> 00:10:04.353
I kill the guards.

104
00:10:04.729 --> 00:10:05.979
I take your two best men

105
00:10:06.022 --> 00:10:09.108
and lead them through the back
streets. which I know well.

106
00:10:09.192 --> 00:10:11.193
and open the front gates.

107
00:10:12.112 --> 00:10:13.529
Then comes the army.

108
00:10:13.696 --> 00:10:16.115
Once the walls are breached.
the city will fall in hours.

109
00:10:16.199 --> 00:10:18.867
Or perhaps you'll lead Grey
Worm and me to the slaughter.

110
00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:21.495
cutting the head off our army.

111
00:10:21.704 --> 00:10:23.539
The masters of Yunkai will pay you your fee

112
00:10:23.665 --> 00:10:25.457
and you won't have to split it three ways

113
00:10:25.542 --> 00:10:27.709
'cause you've already
slaughtered your partners.

114
00:10:27.794 --> 00:10:30.462
You have a very suspicious mind.

115
00:10:30.547 --> 00:10:33.132
In my experience.
only dishonest people think this way.

116
00:10:35.385 --> 00:10:37.553
You command the Unsullied.

117
00:10:38.388 --> 00:10:40.199
What do you think?

118
00:10:40.223 --> 00:10:42.516
You are a leader now.

119
00:10:43.059 --> 00:10:45.936
Do you trust him?

120
00:10:49.107 --> 00:10:51.859
I trust him.

121
00:10:52.986 --> 00:10:54.069
You leave tonight.

122
00:10:54.612 --> 00:10:57.948
Very good. We'll prepare.

123
00:11:03.496 --> 00:11:04.580
Ser Jorah.

124
00:11:06.749 --> 00:11:08.292
You can use an extra sword.

125
00:11:08.793 --> 00:11:12.379
You're the Queensguard.
Ser Barristan. Your place is by the Queen.

126
00:11:13.089 --> 00:11:15.132
If we are truly her loyal servants.

127
00:11:15.258 --> 00:11:17.384
we'll do whatever needs to be done.

128
00:11:17.927 --> 00:11:21.305
no matter the cost. no matter our pride.

129
00:11:24.976 --> 00:11:27.060
We're west of Castle Black.

130
00:11:27.187 --> 00:11:29.271
but the Nightfort's closest to us.

131
00:11:29.689 --> 00:11:32.566
It was the first castle on the Wall.

132
00:11:32.609 --> 00:11:35.986
The Watch abandoned it
during the reign of King Jaehaerys I.

133
00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:39.531
Too big. Impossible to maintain.

134
00:11:39.782 --> 00:11:42.159
Other than Castle Black itself.

135
00:11:42.285 --> 00:11:44.703
the Nightfort's the perfect castle for us.

136
00:11:44.787 --> 00:11:50.667
It's got a secret sally port.
the Black Gate. as old as the Wall itself.

137
00:11:50.752 --> 00:11:54.338
No one's used it in centuries. most likely.

138
00:11:54.547 --> 00:11:59.051
It leads through
the Wall right down into the Nightfort.

139
00:11:59.135 --> 00:12:04.181
if one knows how to find it.
which. it just so happens. I do.

140
00:12:08.895 --> 00:12:11.271
How do you know all that?

141
00:12:11.564 --> 00:12:15.150
I read about it in a very old book.

142
00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:25.369
You know all that
from staring at marks on paper?

143
00:12:26.371 --> 00:12:27.955
Yes.

144
00:12:28.665 --> 00:12:30.999
You're like a wizard.

145
00:12:46.349 --> 00:12:48.183
Our father used to tell us

146
00:12:48.268 --> 00:12:52.187
that no wildling ever looked
upon the Wall and lived.

147
00:12:52.981 --> 00:12:54.731
Here we are.

148
00:12:56.067 --> 00:12:57.651
Alive.

149
00:13:14.043 --> 00:13:16.628
Remember what happens to children who run.

150
00:13:16.754 --> 00:13:19.381
I'm your father and I'll do the talking.

151
00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:31.893
The roads have gone right to hell.

152
00:13:31.936 --> 00:13:33.296
Cracked three spokes this morning.

153
00:13:33.396 --> 00:13:34.730
Need a hand?

154
00:13:34.772 --> 00:13:35.939
Need about eight hands.

155
00:13:36.107 --> 00:13:37.107
Oh!

156
00:13:37.775 --> 00:13:41.820
Got to get this salt pork to the
Twins in time for the wedding.

157
00:13:43.323 --> 00:13:44.614
Many thanks.

158
00:13:47.452 --> 00:13:50.329
Don't! Don't kill him.

159
00:13:50.663 --> 00:13:52.622
Dead rats don't squeak.

160
00:13:52.707 --> 00:13:54.499
You're so dangerous. aren't you?

161
00:13:54.625 --> 00:13:56.418
Saying scary things to little girls.

162
00:13:56.711 --> 00:14:00.630
Killing little boys and old people.
A real hard man you are.

163
00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:02.174
More than anyone you know.

164
00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:03.425
You're wrong.

165
00:14:03.551 --> 00:14:05.594
I know a killer.

166
00:14:05.636 --> 00:14:07.512
- A real killer.
- That so?

167
00:14:07.597 --> 00:14:11.266
You'd be like a kitten to him.
He'd kill you with his little finger.

168
00:14:12.435 --> 00:14:14.436
That him?

169
00:14:15.772 --> 00:14:17.689
- No.
- Good.

170
00:14:18.316 --> 00:14:20.150
Don't kill him.

171
00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.402
Please.

172
00:14:22.987 --> 00:14:24.446
Please don't.

173
00:14:28.034 --> 00:14:31.620
You're very kind.
Someday it'll get you killed.

174
00:14:49.263 --> 00:14:51.139
Where are we?

175
00:14:51.182 --> 00:14:52.933
The Gift. I think.

176
00:14:53.476 --> 00:14:55.143
Brandon the Builder gave all this land

177
00:14:55.269 --> 00:14:56.978
south of the Wall to the Night's Watch

178
00:14:57.063 --> 00:14:59.606
for their sustenance and support.

179
00:15:00.233 --> 00:15:01.983
Maester Luwin taught me that.

180
00:15:04.362 --> 00:15:06.362
Doesn't seem to be supporting
anyone at the moment.

181
00:15:07.281 --> 00:15:09.533
It's good land. and there's no war up here.

182
00:15:10.493 --> 00:15:11.493
Why leave?

183
00:15:11.536 --> 00:15:13.161
Wildlings.

184
00:15:13.788 --> 00:15:15.080
Sorry.

185
00:15:15.832 --> 00:15:19.501
But they come over
the Wall and raid. steal. carry off women.

186
00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:21.670
Old Nan said they turn
your skull into a cup

187
00:15:21.796 --> 00:15:23.839
and make you drink your own blood from it.

188
00:15:26.676 --> 00:15:28.218
That's what Old Nan said.

189
00:15:28.845 --> 00:15:29.928
There's a storm coming.

190
00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.222
I don't see any.

191
00:15:37.395 --> 00:15:38.955
It's as good a place to shelter as any.

192
00:15:42.233 --> 00:15:44.192
We can drink some blood while we wait.

193
00:15:45.027 --> 00:15:46.611
I don't need much.

194
00:15:58.499 --> 00:16:01.001
Only one old man
and eight good horses.

195
00:16:01.043 --> 00:16:03.795
What's one old man doing with eight horses?

196
00:16:04.172 --> 00:16:05.881
He breeds them for the Watch.

197
00:16:05.923 --> 00:16:07.757
How's he keep folks from stealing them?

198
00:16:08.384 --> 00:16:09.968
The Watch protects him.

199
00:16:10.761 --> 00:16:12.637
Not today. they don't.

200
00:16:13.222 --> 00:16:15.474
He's selling horses.
he's got some gold in there.

201
00:16:15.892 --> 00:16:17.058
And proper steel.

202
00:16:17.226 --> 00:16:18.393
Let's carve him up.

203
00:16:18.436 --> 00:16:19.936
We just take the horses and go.

204
00:16:21.063 --> 00:16:22.564
The old man's no threat.

205
00:16:23.858 --> 00:16:25.150
I keep telling you.

206
00:16:25.651 --> 00:16:29.279
He's an old man. A spear through
the heart's a better way to die

207
00:16:29.363 --> 00:16:32.073
than coughing up your
last with no one but your horses to hear.

208
00:16:33.743 --> 00:16:37.245
The Watch might send
a few men looking for a horse thief.

209
00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:40.207
They'll send a lot more
to hunt down murderers.

210
00:16:40.249 --> 00:16:44.961
I hope so.
Killing crows in their castle is tough.

211
00:16:45.046 --> 00:16:48.673
Killing them out
here in the open. that's what we do.

212
00:16:49.509 --> 00:16:52.928
Spread out. Surround the hut and move in.

213
00:17:35.805 --> 00:17:36.846
Ygritte!

214
00:17:39.475 --> 00:17:40.892
Clear the barn!

215
00:18:18.931 --> 00:18:21.531
No one's going to believe
you're a hog farmer if you eat them all.

216
00:18:22.852 --> 00:18:24.769
Best part of the animal.

217
00:18:29.609 --> 00:18:31.276
Don't worry. They're still there.

218
00:18:32.987 --> 00:18:34.362
I know they're still there.

219
00:18:34.572 --> 00:18:38.033
You check every five minutes
like you're afraid they're gonna move.

220
00:18:39.619 --> 00:18:40.702
I'm not afraid.

221
00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:41.995
Of course you are.

222
00:18:43.039 --> 00:18:47.584
You're almost there
and you're afraid you won't make it.

223
00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:51.212
The closer you get.
the worse the fear gets.

224
00:18:51.881 --> 00:18:54.466
No point in trying to
hide behind that face.

225
00:18:55.009 --> 00:18:57.427
I know fear when I see it.

226
00:18:57.511 --> 00:18:59.304
Seen it a lot.

227
00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:02.223
I knew fear when I saw it in you.

228
00:19:04.685 --> 00:19:06.686
You're afraid of fire.

229
00:19:07.897 --> 00:19:09.397
When Beric's sword went up in flames.

230
00:19:09.523 --> 00:19:11.024
you looked like a scared little girl.

231
00:19:15.029 --> 00:19:16.905
And I know why. too.

232
00:19:19.075 --> 00:19:21.242
I heard what your brother did to you.

233
00:19:22.745 --> 00:19:26.373
Pressed your face to the fire like
you're a nice juicy mutton chop.

234
00:19:30.419 --> 00:19:32.253
That give you some ideas?

235
00:19:35.424 --> 00:19:37.300
Might do.

236
00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:42.347
Go ahead. then. You might get away.

237
00:19:43.015 --> 00:19:45.058
Might even make it there on your own.

238
00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:48.228
They're just over the river.

239
00:19:49.105 --> 00:19:51.356
The closest you've been to family

240
00:19:51.482 --> 00:19:53.775
since llyn Payne snipped your daddy's neck.

241
00:19:57.530 --> 00:19:59.572
Someday I'll put a sword through

242
00:19:59.699 --> 00:20:01.741
your eye and out the back of your skull.

243
00:20:26.934 --> 00:20:29.144
How are we going to get past the Wall?

244
00:20:30.146 --> 00:20:32.480
My uncle said it's 700 feet high.

245
00:20:37.611 --> 00:20:38.820
How did you get past it?

246
00:20:43.492 --> 00:20:45.869
Got in a boat and rowed
past the Bay of Seals.

247
00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:49.247
It would take us two months
to get to the Bay of Seals.

248
00:20:49.457 --> 00:20:51.082
Some climb straight up the ice.

249
00:20:51.167 --> 00:20:52.792
Even Hodor's not strong enough to

250
00:20:52.918 --> 00:20:54.544
climb the Wall with me on his back.

251
00:20:54.628 --> 00:20:55.670
Hodor.

252
00:20:58.048 --> 00:21:00.341
Nineteen castles guard the Wall.

253
00:21:00.426 --> 00:21:01.528
Only three are still manned.

254
00:21:01.552 --> 00:21:02.632
Hodor!

255
00:21:03.679 --> 00:21:05.907
One of those abandoned
fortresses will give us a way through.

256
00:21:05.931 --> 00:21:07.849
My uncle said the gates
were sealed with ice

257
00:21:07.975 --> 00:21:09.851
and stone when the castles were deserted.

258
00:21:10.352 --> 00:21:12.479
Well. we'll have to open them up again.

259
00:21:13.856 --> 00:21:15.815
Whoa. whoa. whoa!

260
00:21:15.858 --> 00:21:17.275
There's a rider out there.

261
00:21:19.069 --> 00:21:20.570
Just one?

262
00:21:20.654 --> 00:21:22.405
- There's more.
- Hodor!

263
00:21:25.367 --> 00:21:26.701
It's just thunder. sweet giant.

264
00:21:26.827 --> 00:21:28.161
Hodor.

265
00:21:28.662 --> 00:21:30.538
I yield.

266
00:21:30.623 --> 00:21:32.165
- I yield.
- Wildlings.

267
00:21:37.505 --> 00:21:38.797
Where's Shaggydog and Summer?

268
00:21:38.881 --> 00:21:39.964
Hunting.

269
00:21:40.883 --> 00:21:42.926
Hodor!

270
00:21:43.803 --> 00:21:45.178
- Shh. Quiet. Hodor.
- Hodor!

271
00:21:45.221 --> 00:21:47.263
Make him shut up. If they hear us...

272
00:21:47.348 --> 00:21:48.784
Hush. Hodor. No... No more Hodoring.

273
00:21:48.808 --> 00:21:50.225
Hodor!

274
00:21:50.309 --> 00:21:51.976
- Hodor!
- Hodor. calm down.

275
00:21:52.061 --> 00:21:54.021
- You need to keep quiet.
- They're gonna hear us.

276
00:21:54.396 --> 00:21:55.939
Hodor. be quiet.

277
00:21:57.650 --> 00:21:59.567
- Hodor!
- Hodor. calm down.

278
00:21:59.652 --> 00:22:01.027
Hodor! Hodor!

279
00:22:01.153 --> 00:22:02.529
Hodor. be quiet!

280
00:22:25.427 --> 00:22:26.636
What did you do?

281
00:22:27.304 --> 00:22:29.055
Nothing.

282
00:22:29.557 --> 00:22:31.182
I don't know.

283
00:22:36.522 --> 00:22:37.772
What's that?

284
00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:40.441
That's a horse dying.

285
00:22:50.703 --> 00:22:52.954
Bring them over here.

286
00:22:53.539 --> 00:22:56.082
That was
the last of them. The rest are dead.

287
00:22:56.625 --> 00:22:58.710
I heard shouting up there.

288
00:22:58.878 --> 00:23:00.086
Thunder.

289
00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:03.089
I know the difference
between shouting and thunder.

290
00:23:03.716 --> 00:23:05.967
Maybe it's ghosts.

291
00:23:16.478 --> 00:23:19.063
That won't help you. grandpa.

292
00:23:23.611 --> 00:23:24.944
Where you riding?

293
00:23:25.362 --> 00:23:27.071
Doesn't matter now. does it?

294
00:23:27.156 --> 00:23:29.574
No. it doesn't matter now.

295
00:23:31.535 --> 00:23:34.662
Cut his throat.
or he'll tell the crows we're here.

296
00:23:41.211 --> 00:23:42.378
You understand.

297
00:23:43.005 --> 00:23:44.297
Let me stand at least.

298
00:23:45.591 --> 00:23:47.759
Let me go with a bit of dignity.

299
00:23:53.098 --> 00:23:54.474
Make the crow kill him.

300
00:23:58.354 --> 00:24:01.439
You're one of us now. Prove it.

301
00:24:06.195 --> 00:24:07.695
The wolves are out there.

302
00:24:11.575 --> 00:24:12.992
I can't do it by choice.

303
00:24:13.702 --> 00:24:15.161
I don't know how.

304
00:24:15.496 --> 00:24:17.121
It happens in my dreams.

305
00:24:17.456 --> 00:24:20.041
You're a warg. Bran. It's in your blood.

306
00:24:21.877 --> 00:24:22.877
I can't.

307
00:24:23.212 --> 00:24:25.046
You just did. with him.

308
00:24:25.547 --> 00:24:26.947
A wolf is nothing compared to that.

309
00:24:35.057 --> 00:24:36.140
She looks sharp.

310
00:24:46.193 --> 00:24:50.321
Do it.

311
00:24:50.656 --> 00:24:53.449
I told you. He's still one of them.

312
00:24:55.911 --> 00:24:57.161
Go on. boy.

313
00:25:00.374 --> 00:25:01.708
Go on!

314
00:25:10.968 --> 00:25:13.594
He's a crow. He'll always be a crow.

315
00:25:14.054 --> 00:25:16.472
And here's his crow wife guarding him.

316
00:25:16.807 --> 00:25:19.600
He'll stab us in the back
first chance he gets.

317
00:25:22.604 --> 00:25:24.105
Kill him.

318
00:25:39.997 --> 00:25:41.122
He's one of them.

319
00:25:41.248 --> 00:25:42.373
No!

320
00:25:42.458 --> 00:25:44.292
Do you hear me? Ahh!

321
00:25:50.340 --> 00:25:53.384
You're not gonna die for one of them.

322
00:25:54.970 --> 00:25:56.179
Do it.

323
00:25:57.514 --> 00:25:59.432
They'll find us if you don't.

324
00:26:29.171 --> 00:26:31.005
You were right the whole time.

325
00:27:18.220 --> 00:27:20.388
When you hear
a songbird's whistle. you come.

326
00:27:21.014 --> 00:27:24.684
I'm a great whistler.
The greatest in the land.

327
00:27:30.566 --> 00:27:32.233
Daario Naharis.

328
00:28:00.762 --> 00:28:02.138
That one was quick.

329
00:28:05.434 --> 00:28:07.476
- There may be others.
- I doubt it.

330
00:28:07.561 --> 00:28:10.521
The Yunkish prefer to let their
slaves do their fighting for them.

331
00:28:55.275 --> 00:28:56.943
That's what you call a few guards?

332
00:29:22.261 --> 00:29:24.512
Come on! What do you got. huh?

333
00:30:38.712 --> 00:30:40.546
Lord Edmure.

334
00:30:42.799 --> 00:30:45.092
I hope I'm not a disappointment to you.

335
00:30:54.144 --> 00:30:56.437
You're a delight to me. my lady.

336
00:30:57.939 --> 00:31:01.233
You may now cloak the bride and
bring her under your protection.

337
00:31:30.597 --> 00:31:35.184
In the sight of the Seven.
I hereby seal these two souls.

338
00:31:36.228 --> 00:31:39.647
binding them as one for eternity.

339
00:31:39.731 --> 00:31:42.400
Look upon each other and say the words.

340
00:31:45.445 --> 00:31:47.279
- Father. Smith...
- Father. Smith...

341
00:31:47.322 --> 00:31:49.698
- Warrior. Mother...
- Warrior. Mother...

342
00:31:49.783 --> 00:31:52.827
- Maiden. Crone. Stranger.
- Maiden. Crone. Stranger.

343
00:31:53.495 --> 00:31:55.162
- I am hers...
- I am his...

344
00:31:55.205 --> 00:31:57.206
- and she is mine...
- and he is mine...

345
00:31:57.290 --> 00:32:00.751
From this day
until the end of my days.

346
00:32:06.007 --> 00:32:07.341
Is that safe?

347
00:32:07.509 --> 00:32:08.884
They're long gone.

348
00:32:14.015 --> 00:32:15.307
You were right.

349
00:32:15.350 --> 00:32:18.477
I can get inside
Summer's mind whenever I want.

350
00:32:18.520 --> 00:32:20.229
Of course you can.

351
00:32:21.481 --> 00:32:23.315
North of the Wall there are wildlings

352
00:32:23.442 --> 00:32:25.276
who can control all sorts of animals.

353
00:32:26.778 --> 00:32:28.362
But you did a lot more than that.

354
00:32:30.574 --> 00:32:32.783
You got inside Hodor's mind.

355
00:32:34.661 --> 00:32:36.141
They can't do that north of the Wall?

356
00:32:38.790 --> 00:32:41.709
No one can do that. Anywhere.

357
00:32:48.800 --> 00:32:51.093
When I was looking through Summer's eyes.

358
00:32:51.178 --> 00:32:52.761
- I saw Jon.
- Where?

359
00:32:52.846 --> 00:32:54.096
He was with the wildlings.

360
00:32:54.639 --> 00:32:56.474
They tried to kill him. but he got away.

361
00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:58.560
He'll be heading back
to Castle Black. then.

362
00:32:59.102 --> 00:33:00.227
That's where we should go.

363
00:33:00.312 --> 00:33:02.730
For all we know.
Castle Black's already under attack.

364
00:33:03.148 --> 00:33:04.375
If this many wildlings got through...

365
00:33:04.399 --> 00:33:05.483
I already told you.

366
00:33:05.901 --> 00:33:07.401
I'm not going north of the Wall.

367
00:33:08.570 --> 00:33:10.362
Everything Jojen told me is true.

368
00:33:12.699 --> 00:33:14.658
You saw what I did to Hodor.

369
00:33:14.910 --> 00:33:16.744
I have to find the three-eyed raven.

370
00:33:16.828 --> 00:33:18.329
Listen to me. little lord.

371
00:33:18.413 --> 00:33:19.622
Don't worry.

372
00:33:20.457 --> 00:33:22.583
I'm not asking you to come with me.

373
00:33:24.920 --> 00:33:26.337
It won't be safe for Rickon.

374
00:33:27.088 --> 00:33:29.507
Me? I'm coming with you.

375
00:33:29.591 --> 00:33:31.133
No.

376
00:33:31.801 --> 00:33:34.512
You and Osha and Shaggydog
head for the Last Hearth.

377
00:33:34.679 --> 00:33:37.848
The Umbers are our bannermen.
They'll protect you.

378
00:33:37.933 --> 00:33:42.937
I'm coming with you.
I'm your brother. I have to protect you.

379
00:33:46.274 --> 00:33:48.984
Right now I have to protect you.

380
00:33:49.694 --> 00:33:52.655
Robb's at war and I'm
going beyond the Wall.

381
00:33:52.739 --> 00:33:55.783
If something happens to us.
you're the heir to Winterfell.

382
00:33:59.162 --> 00:34:01.080
Would you know how to find the Last Hearth?

383
00:34:01.122 --> 00:34:04.583
You Southerners
build your big castles and you never move.

384
00:34:04.626 --> 00:34:05.960
You're easy to find.

385
00:34:06.628 --> 00:34:08.837
We're not Southerners.

386
00:34:09.881 --> 00:34:11.840
And I don't want to leave you.

387
00:34:11.925 --> 00:34:12.925
Shh!

388
00:34:13.009 --> 00:34:14.969
Come here. little soldier.

389
00:34:16.179 --> 00:34:19.348
You and me.
we're gonna have some adventures.

390
00:34:20.267 --> 00:34:22.017
You don't have to do any of this.

391
00:34:23.562 --> 00:34:27.273
Your family took me in
and was good to me without cause.

392
00:34:29.901 --> 00:34:32.152
We'll be fine. you and me.

393
00:34:32.237 --> 00:34:36.282
The Umbers are great warriors. Even I
heard about them growing up.

394
00:34:37.325 --> 00:34:39.368
They'll teach you how to swing a sword.

395
00:34:40.161 --> 00:34:42.663
I know how to swing a sword.

396
00:34:49.921 --> 00:34:52.631
You're leaving now?
It's the middle of the night.

397
00:34:52.674 --> 00:34:54.258
I learned to walk in darkness.

398
00:34:57.262 --> 00:34:58.502
Say your good-byes. little man.

399
00:35:07.022 --> 00:35:08.689
Keep this one safe.

400
00:35:11.234 --> 00:35:12.526
He means the world to me.

401
00:35:34.174 --> 00:35:36.508
We've been waiting a long time.

402
00:35:38.637 --> 00:35:40.304
Haven't we?

403
00:35:41.640 --> 00:35:43.390
Well. I don't know. you tell me.

404
00:35:43.558 --> 00:35:45.309
How long does it take to sack a city?

405
00:35:54.069 --> 00:35:55.819
It was just as you said.

406
00:35:56.404 --> 00:35:59.156
They did not believe until it was too late.

407
00:35:59.240 --> 00:36:04.578
Their slave soldiers
threw down their spears and surrendered.

408
00:36:09.209 --> 00:36:11.251
And Daario Naharis?

409
00:36:32.232 --> 00:36:34.483
The city is yours. my queen.

410
00:36:57.757 --> 00:36:59.174
They're good. aren't they?

411
00:36:59.259 --> 00:37:00.444
They ought to be because they cost enough.

412
00:37:08.476 --> 00:37:10.310
Look at the crowd there.

413
00:37:15.442 --> 00:37:16.984
He complained about this marriage

414
00:37:17.026 --> 00:37:19.278
the entire ride from Riverrun.

415
00:37:19.320 --> 00:37:20.612
and now look at him.

416
00:37:20.655 --> 00:37:22.865
The Gods love to reward a fool.

417
00:37:23.199 --> 00:37:24.575
- Uncle.
- What?

418
00:37:25.368 --> 00:37:30.456
He's my nephew. I love him.
And he's a damned fool.

419
00:37:35.879 --> 00:37:37.921
Don't you drink. Lord Bolton?

420
00:37:38.006 --> 00:37:40.466
Never do. my lady. Dulls the senses.

421
00:37:40.508 --> 00:37:42.509
That's the point.

422
00:37:42.594 --> 00:37:44.636
Didn't you marry one of these Frey girls?

423
00:37:44.679 --> 00:37:48.432
Aye. Lord Walder
let me choose any of his granddaughters

424
00:37:48.933 --> 00:37:52.519
and promised me
the girl's weight in silver as a dowry.

425
00:37:52.604 --> 00:37:54.271
So I have a fat young bride.

426
00:37:56.274 --> 00:37:58.192
I hope she makes you very happy.

427
00:37:58.276 --> 00:38:00.027
Well. she's made me very rich.

428
00:38:00.361 --> 00:38:05.115
Pardon. my lord.
my lady. I need to find a tree to piss on.

429
00:38:07.535 --> 00:38:11.121
My mother's alone
with Roose Bolton. I should rescue her.

430
00:38:11.206 --> 00:38:14.708
Your mother is less in need of rescue
than any woman I've ever met.

431
00:38:15.084 --> 00:38:18.045
Be kind. She's finally
starting to like you.

432
00:38:19.964 --> 00:38:21.548
And I like her.

433
00:38:21.633 --> 00:38:24.968
But if she had her way.
I would be back in Volantis

434
00:38:25.053 --> 00:38:28.305
playing my harp
and you would be sitting over there.

435
00:38:28.556 --> 00:38:31.350
eating blackberries out
of Roslin Frey's hand.

436
00:38:31.434 --> 00:38:33.477
Perhaps I've made a terrible mistake.

437
00:38:36.481 --> 00:38:39.149
Striking your king is an act of treason.

438
00:38:42.570 --> 00:38:43.987
No. don't.

439
00:38:45.824 --> 00:38:46.824
Don't insult them.

440
00:38:49.786 --> 00:38:51.578
Your Grace.

441
00:38:58.628 --> 00:39:02.589
The septon has prayed his prayers.

442
00:39:02.632 --> 00:39:04.591
some words were said.

443
00:39:04.634 --> 00:39:09.471
and Lord Edmure
has wrapped my daughter in a cloak.

444
00:39:09.556 --> 00:39:13.892
But they are not yet man and wife.

445
00:39:13.935 --> 00:39:15.769
A sword needs a sheath.

446
00:39:22.819 --> 00:39:24.152
And a wedding needs a bedding.

447
00:39:26.322 --> 00:39:28.073
What does my sire say?

448
00:39:28.116 --> 00:39:31.034
To bed! To bed! To bed!

449
00:39:36.749 --> 00:39:40.919
If you think the time is right.
Lord Walder. by all means.

450
00:39:42.046 --> 00:39:43.088
let us bed them.

451
00:39:50.138 --> 00:39:52.764
To bed! To bed! To bed!

452
00:39:58.771 --> 00:40:00.188
Go on.

453
00:40:18.541 --> 00:40:19.750
Ho-ho!

454
00:40:20.001 --> 00:40:21.793
Careful now. ladies.

455
00:40:21.836 --> 00:40:23.837
Once you set that monster free.

456
00:40:23.963 --> 00:40:25.964
there's no caging him again.

457
00:40:27.717 --> 00:40:30.802
To bed! To bed! To bed!

458
00:40:33.598 --> 00:40:35.432
Poor girl.

459
00:40:35.516 --> 00:40:38.226
Every bride suffers the same.

460
00:40:38.311 --> 00:40:40.771
I'm sure you endured yours with grace.

461
00:40:40.855 --> 00:40:42.856
Oh. Ned forbade it.

462
00:40:43.441 --> 00:40:46.443
He said it wouldn't be right if he
broke a man's jaw on our wedding night.

463
00:40:55.203 --> 00:40:58.205
That is a very strange custom.

464
00:40:58.706 --> 00:41:02.042
I suppose it does seem strange
from a foreigner's perspective.

465
00:41:02.085 --> 00:41:03.543
It seems normal to you?

466
00:41:04.712 --> 00:41:05.963
It's a tradition.

467
00:41:08.257 --> 00:41:10.717
Without the bedding ceremony.
there's no real proof

468
00:41:10.760 --> 00:41:12.594
the lord and lady
consummated their marriage.

469
00:41:12.679 --> 00:41:16.723
No. but there
are other ways of providing proof.

470
00:41:19.310 --> 00:41:20.727
Boy or girl?

471
00:41:23.648 --> 00:41:25.148
I don't know.

472
00:41:25.233 --> 00:41:28.068
But if it's a boy.
I know what we should name him.

473
00:41:28.152 --> 00:41:29.820
Oh. do you?

474
00:41:30.571 --> 00:41:33.782
It seems to me the father
should have some say in his son's naming.

475
00:41:33.866 --> 00:41:35.075
Eddard.

476
00:41:39.205 --> 00:41:43.417
Don't you want to
teach little Ned Stark how to ride horses?

477
00:41:43.751 --> 00:41:45.460
I do.

478
00:42:41.851 --> 00:42:43.727
Go on. line 'em up!

479
00:43:00.828 --> 00:43:02.329
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa.

480
00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:07.125
Where are you going?

481
00:43:07.543 --> 00:43:09.169
Got salt pork for the feast.

482
00:43:09.253 --> 00:43:10.587
The feast is over.

483
00:43:12.048 --> 00:43:14.007
Doesn't sound like it's over.

484
00:43:14.092 --> 00:43:16.927
If I tell you it's over. it's over.

485
00:43:17.720 --> 00:43:21.348
Turn this cart around
and get the hell out of here.

486
00:43:21.390 --> 00:43:23.016
Got pig's feet. too.

487
00:43:24.519 --> 00:43:28.021
Are you soft in the head?
Turn this cart around.

488
00:43:40.993 --> 00:43:42.369
Your Grace.

489
00:43:48.543 --> 00:43:54.673
I feel I've been remiss in my duties.

490
00:43:54.882 --> 00:43:58.135
I've given you meat and wine and music.

491
00:43:58.219 --> 00:44:03.723
but I haven't shown you
the hospitality you deserve.

492
00:44:05.143 --> 00:44:09.688
My king has married
and I owe my new queen a wedding gift.

493
00:44:14.777 --> 00:44:15.777
Robb!

494
00:44:31.752 --> 00:44:32.794
Ohh!

495
00:44:34.881 --> 00:44:36.756
Ahh!

496
00:44:37.967 --> 00:44:39.259
Ahh!

497
00:45:03.117 --> 00:45:06.286
You ready to head home to Winterfell. eh?

498
00:45:09.749 --> 00:45:11.082
Feast over yet. is it?

499
00:45:11.125 --> 00:45:12.125
Aye. it's over.

500
00:45:48.287 --> 00:45:49.829
Aim!

501
00:46:19.193 --> 00:46:20.193
It's too late.

502
00:47:02.403 --> 00:47:05.572
The King in the North arises.

503
00:47:27.219 --> 00:47:28.219
Lord Walder!

504
00:47:29.263 --> 00:47:30.847
Lord Walder. enough!

505
00:47:31.390 --> 00:47:33.266
Let it end!

506
00:47:35.269 --> 00:47:39.189
Please. He is my son.

507
00:47:39.648 --> 00:47:41.608
My first son.

508
00:47:41.692 --> 00:47:44.194
Let him go.
and I swear that we will forget this.

509
00:47:44.570 --> 00:47:46.154
I swear it by the Old Gods and New.

510
00:47:47.031 --> 00:47:48.531
We will take no vengeance.

511
00:47:48.616 --> 00:47:52.160
You already swore me
one oath right here in my castle.

512
00:47:52.244 --> 00:47:55.955
You swore by all the Gods
your son would marry my daughter!

513
00:47:55.998 --> 00:47:59.459
Take me
for a hostage. but let Robb go.

514
00:47:59.960 --> 00:48:03.296
Robb. get up. Get up and walk out.

515
00:48:04.173 --> 00:48:09.469
Please!

516
00:48:10.137 --> 00:48:14.432
And why would I let him do that?

517
00:48:16.936 --> 00:48:18.770
On my honor as a Tully.

518
00:48:19.730 --> 00:48:22.190
on my honor as a Stark.

519
00:48:22.983 --> 00:48:28.405
let him go.
or I will cut your wife's throat.

520
00:48:36.664 --> 00:48:39.165
I'll find another.

521
00:48:42.211 --> 00:48:44.129
Mother.

522
00:48:45.673 --> 00:48:47.340
The Lannisters send their regards.

522
